# Consoles 1 and 2 at 16777216/280896 frames a second, chained through
# console 1's two ports, save inside an advance; console 0 at 60000/1001
# promises one step ahead and paces the scenario. Consoles 1 and 2 are both
# parked inside a frame at 270, with messages in flight, so the save holds
# their advances and the from and rewound runs make them again. Both are
# parked at 600 as well, so the rewound run abandons their frames before it
# loads, and every run abandons them before it unloads the cores. Their
# input scripts give each frame around the one saved a mask of its own: a
# frame finished after a load with another frame's input fails those runs.
console 0 core=test
console 1 core=test
console 2 core=test
option 0 link_test_fps 60000/1001
option 0 link_test_rate_0 60000
option 0 link_test_lookahead_0 1
option 1 link_test_ports 2
option 1 link_test_fps 16777216/280896
option 1 link_test_rate_0 16777216
option 1 link_test_rate_1 16777216
option 1 link_test_save_in_advance on
option 2 link_test_fps 16777216/280896
option 2 link_test_rate_0 16777216
option 2 link_test_save_in_advance on
input 1 0 spans_save_in_advance_c1.inp
input 2 0 spans_save_in_advance_c2.inp
0 cable 0:0 1:0
0 cable 1:1 2:0
270 save mid
270 checkpoint in_flight
600 checkpoint last
600 end
